    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0186" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.00/664: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-17T19:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                                1920—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 18—6:33
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1567. Took up question of communication with Monrovia as directed in your 1376,
                    August 16, 4 p.m., with M. de Peretti<anchor n="17" xml:id="d65-f1"/> this
                    afternoon. He promised to investigate and accord every facility. He also agreed
                    to instruct French representative in sense desired.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d65-f1" n="17" xml:id="d65-f1-content">
                <p>E. M. J. de Peretti, Director of Political and Commercial Affairs, French Foreign
                    Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
